    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40962" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕlĕvātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναιώρημα</span> (Hippoc.), <i>scum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut urina nullam faciat relevationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 5, 3, 55</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A lightening</i>, <i>alleviation</i>,
				<i>relief</i> (postclass. and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oneris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad M. Caes. 4, 13</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b> (opp. gravatio), <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 5, 10, 96</span></i>; Octav.
				<i><span class="en">Hor. 1, 9</span></i>.</div>
